  set (a key change there is lost when the set updates): see docs/SPACES.md, "Read-only"

song data
- chart editor (fix a typo in place): plan in docs/VARIANTS.md, "Editing a chart", not built
- the import page's "Create New Setlist" may offer the people of the space the app is in, not the one being
  imported into: getSpacePeople now takes the database, but still reads the current space too; check
- at import, when the chart's CCLI number finds a song and a song with no CCLI number has the same title,
  offer to link that one as a variant too (the library repair and "Merge another song into this one" do
  it afterwards: docs/VARIANTS.md, "Versions and merging")
- mark what differs in the chart comparison (the import page's Compare tabs, docs/VARIANTS.md): give
  song-section a `highlight` input (`chords`, `words`, `only`) that draws a coloured bar down the
  section's edge and a small note, in theme colours, so the charts keep the normal rendering. The
  values come from `compareCharts(...).stanzas` (each stanza of one chart marked against the other's, by
  position in the chart). Pass them down through song-display by section index. Not needed until the
  plain comparison proves hard to read
- the library repair's preview should show the comparison for the songs it merges (docs/VARIANTS.md,
  "Importing a chart the library already has", item 5)
- variants of one song are all labelled "Original" after a copy between spaces: label them by what
  differs (the key, say) or ask
- a free-form source (who wrote a chart) can be supplied nowhere: add an optional field to the import
  and to the song's info
- feature idea: song structure.  Have an translucent overlay on the top right
  that shows intended structure vertically e.g. "v1 c1 v2 c2 x2 b1 x4 c1". We
  could fill in a default by guessing based on source chordpro, but users
  should be able to edit it per setlists, as they might structure things
  differently.  
- feature idea (raised 2026-10-30): a current rotation. Leaders and admins mark a set of songs as in the
  current rotation, and manage them; a team can then curate its official song list formally. Decide with it
  who may add songs to a Team and what a PA/media team may do: today only a worship leader and above
  (writer) can import songs that sync (a team member's import stays on their device, never sent), and
  the invite defaults to worship leader. Importing a chart could stay open to anyone, since it only makes
  the chart available; being in the rotation is the curated part



