- what ZAP's first baseline found (2026-10-25): no Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS, in infra/TODO),
  then make rule 10035 FAIL in .zap/rules.tsv; no
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy / Embedder-Policy (rule 90004), which need trying against Google sign-in
  and the Picker, whose windows and frames COEP can break; responses with no Content-Type (10019, which
  ones: the report in the DAST run's artifact); its caching warnings (10015, 10049), mostly meant
  (the service worker, fresh API answers), to be looked at once and the rules set to match

live mode
 - loading a setlist at a song (reload, or a link to #song-N) reports the song, then the
   overview, then the song again (the section observer's first callback): the media
   player is told "no song" in between, and for that moment the edit button and arrow
   keys act on the overview. tests/live.playwright.ts opens songs with the arrow instead
 - follow the leader's current song/section in a live session (after live sync; an optional `current` in the live setlist)

tests
 - tests/songs.playwright.ts "choosing a song opens it at its own URL, and back returns to the
   list" failed twice in full runs (not alone, 8 of 8 passed): undiagnosed, so not in
   docs/test-catches.jsonl. Run it with --repeat-each under load to find the cause
 - coverage of the end-to-end tests: `just coverage` merges the node and browser unit suites only,
   and neither the floor nor docs/stats.jsonl has any for e2e. Playwright can collect V8 coverage
   from Chromium-based browsers (page.coverage; not WebKit), to be turned into
   lcov (v8-to-istanbul, a new dependency, or a script of our own) and merged by scripts/coverage.ts
   like the other two, from CI's Linux e2e job as an artifact. Mind that e2e coverage varies with
   timing more than the unit suites' (the floor would need a run or two that agree to lower it)

ccli import
 - adding the same song twice to a setlist should be prevented (decided): the add-song modal, import and any other
   way in say it is already in this set instead of adding it
 - try importing in original key, but record the key that it was set to in the songselect page, and add to setlist in that key
  - handle numbers on import (need to get an original key)
 - make it reuse open windows for import (maybe need to get the default app, not opened via import, to have the tag tag?)
 - email import is built (docs/EMAIL_IMPORT.md): the parser, the /import-setlist review page, the email Worker
  with its rate limits, matching by CCLI number, title and words. Other ways in are not worth building: Share To
  (email apps do not share an email to a web app), a pasted link (the reply's link opens the installed app), and
  WhatsApp, which shares neither text messages nor a selection of them
- email import, from surveying 61 real emails (tests/emails-private.node.test.ts): about half the
  charts have no CCLI number. They are old OnSong PDFs from before SongSelect, which people still
  use: a different version of the song, often under another title. So a chart with no CCLI number
  must not be taken as the song: match the title against the library first (and the other
  databases), and offer replacing it with the SongSelect version, which is how the library stays
  one shared set. Leaders also write the key with no "in" ("Behold him Bb"), number the PDFs'
  filenames to give the order, and put a note or a second title in brackets.
- email import, later: mass-import the emails that matched no setlist as new historic setlists, once the import works
  properly: the leader, date and songs from importFromEmail, songs matched to the library by
  CCLI number then title, with shells and SongSelect links for the rest. Many have no date (events
  like "Prayer Day"), so it must ask.
- notes on a setlist song (SetlistEntry.notes, the older plain-text note) are not shown or edited anywhere: show
  them with the annotations (docs/ANNOTATIONS.md, "Not built yet"), or drop the field. The email import fills them in
  ("fairly empty to start", "May also be in E")

sharing
- share links: built (docs/SHARING.md): create/update/stop from a share button in the overview header (a modal with the link and QR code),
  QR code, sync keeps them current and ends them, /s/<id> opens one read-only and offline.
  Tried on several devices, with no account and offline (2026-10-16). Not tried against a
  Workspace account.
- share links, later: key changes and other view settings on a received set are lost when it
  updates; keep them per device.
- share links, later: an "Add songs to my library" action on the share page (and for the
  whole setlist), importing through incoming-songs.ts. It's the sharer's job to hold the
  rights. This breaks the "never mixed into a library" rule in docs/SHARING.md, so update
  that when it's built. Not part of the first version.
- team spaces for people with no Google account (raised 2026-10-19): members sign in to the Worker with a Google
  ID token, so any Google account (not only Gmail or Workspace) can join, but not a person with none. Idea, later,
  opt-in per team space: a read-only invite link (the Worker keeps a hash of a random token with the reader role and
  accepts it in place of an ID token for reads, fetching through the owner's token; writes refused; edits stay on
  the reader's device). Needs expiry, revoking one invite, a warning that the link is a bearer credential (it reads
  the whole library, unlike a one-setlist share link), and no per-person identity. Share links and "Shared with me"
  already cover a volunteer who only needs this week's set

 - the pad sets are the user's own (Drive): the app ships none, so pads are off until one is
   uploaded (the first upload is chosen)
 - keep cached pads in their own Storage Bucket (navigator.storageBuckets, Chromium
   only), marked expendable, so the browser can evict pads without the setlists and
   songs. Pads re-download from Drive. Fall back to the default caches elsewhere.

UI
- recover when Safari has cleared the storage (the server keeps the sign-in blob in a cookie), and an install nag that
  insists on iOS: both are plans in docs/OFFLINE_STORAGE.md, with the usage they are for (an iPad opened every 3 to 4
  weeks, on poor wifi). The first needs an auth review before it is built

- email replies: a logo where Gmail shows a profile picture needs BIMI, and BIMI needs a VMC or CMC
  certificate (from a CA such as DigiCert or Entrust, a yearly cost; Let's Encrypt cannot issue it).
  Without one Gmail shows the letter circle. The other parts: a DNS TXT at default._bimi.chordless.app
  pointing at an SVG Tiny PS logo served over HTTPS (public/ would do), DMARC at p=quarantine or
  reject, and SPF/DKIM that align with the domain (check that Cloudflare signs the Worker's replies
  with the domain's own DKIM key: not known). Not worth it for one church team; revisit if a
  certificate is bought for another reason.

library
 - lyrics full-text search is built (docs/SEARCH.md). Not built: matchLibrary's "line of the words" step still scans
   instead of using the index; a stored index if libraries grow; ranking a title that is the word above one that has
   it; apostrophe contractions and ends of words ("singin'")
 - ccli report nag

- Make the settings controls and panels (About: version, install, offline, storage status) more compact; they are all a little large.
- The info icon is an i-in-a-circle inside a second circle. Want one circle only: either just an `i` inside our current border circle, or the icon without the border.
- Shared with me (docs/SHARING.md, "Shared with me"): built the database, the home page group, and tidying (expiry, and dropping a setlist once the user has it in a space). Search across all databases (library page and add-song modal, tagged "From …") and "Add to my library" (a copy into the current space) are built. Still to do: deleting received songs by hand; warnings on space delete/Reset from Drive. Links are shorter (128-bit key + 6-character setlist code that sends space members straight to their own setlist).
- server-sent invite emails: decided against for now (docs/SPACES.md, "Invites are for an email address"); the share sheet / WhatsApp / Gmail buttons cover it. Revisit if links get lost, after rate limits
